 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You build a city street, with a big water pipe buried underneath. Simple.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Cars drive over it all day, and the pipe carries water to every house.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the pipe gets old. A tiny crack opens, and water starts leaking into the soil.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The water washes the sand away, grain by grain, into the cracks of the pipes.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "From above, the asphalt looks perfect. Underneath, a hole keeps growing.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then one morning, the road just drops into the ground.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "In 2025, a burst pipe in Bangkok helped open a pit about fifty meters deep, right in front of a hospital.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So first, you fill the hole with crushed rock, packed down layer by layer.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then you swap the old pipe for a flexible one that bends instead of cracking.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "You add sensors that listen to the pipe, so the hiss of a leak sends an alert.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And trucks with ground radar scan under the road, looking for empty pockets.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "If they find one, crews fill it before anyone notices a thing.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then you put fresh asphalt back on top, and the cars roll again.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a street that warns you before it falls. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
